        "4": {
          "id": "4",
          "name": "progression.md",
          "language": "md",
          "contents": "# Lesson 8 · Student Film Festival Organizer\nGoal: build and check a simple search for short films, then validate it.\n\n## App basics\n- Search box matches **title**, **genre**, and **vibes**.\n- Optional operators inside the box:\n  - `genre:comedy` filters to a single genre.\n  - `len:short` or `len:medium` or `len:long` filters by length group.\n- The status line shows **match count**, **total minutes**, and whether it **fits** the block.\n\n---\n\n## Part A · Implement & explain\n1. Read the search code: `searchFilms(items, query)` splits the query into tokens and uses AND logic.\n2. In your own words, explain where a token can match: title, genre, or vibes.\n3. Try three queries and record totals:\n   - `quiet`  \n   - `genre:documentary calm`  \n   - `len:short`\n\n---\n\n## Part B · Debug\n1. Break it on purpose: search with `len:SHORT` and notice it fails.  \n   Fix: the app expects lowercase; note how you would handle case-insensitive values.\n2. Try a query with an extra comma: `quiet, , comedy`.  \n   Check that empty tokens are ignored. If not, patch the split/trim logic.\n3. Confirm that every keyword must match somewhere (AND).  \n   Example: `quiet space` likely narrows the list a lot. Is that expected?\n\n---\n\n## Part C · Validate with AI test cases\nAsk an AI to propose compact tests.\n\n**Prompt**\n> Create five queries for a student film list that uses: title, genre, vibes; operators genre: and len: (short|medium|long). For each, give the expected **count** and the expected **total minutes** based on the data I describe next. Output as a table with columns: query | expected_count | expected_minutes. Keep queries short.\n\nThen paste the dataset (title, minutes, genre, vibes) and run the tests in the app. If a result disagrees, note why and fix the search if needed.\n\n---\n\n## Part D · Edge cases & refinements\n- Add case-insensitive handling for `genre:` and `len:` values.\n- Allow `OR` with a vertical bar in one token: `quiet|calm` (treat it as either word).\n- Prevent negative numbers in the block field.  \n- Optional: show a tiny warning when a single film is longer than the block.\n\n---\n\n## Exit ticket\nWrite two lines:\n1) What change made your search more reliable?  \n2) One query where AND logic helped and one where it felt too strict.\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
